@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch15ch16-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch15ch16-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 15 and 16"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch15ch16-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch15ch16_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.0.0 (2026-11-11): Mission stage. Opened as its own narrow lineage, same pattern as Lineage3 (ch09ch10), Lineage4 (ch11ch12) and Lineage5 (ch13ch14), per the owner's standing rule to prefer simple, narrow, closeable lineages, and the owner's instruction this conversation ('Let's proceed with next 2 chapters in order'), which is chapters 15-16 per the file-verified chapter count given the previous turn. ORDINAL CHECK (lineage-practice-lessons.md discipline, applied again after the real collision found and ruled on for Lineage5): scanned the latest version of every narrow-lineage file (sen0414_ch09ch10_lineage_v1_7_0.ttl: Lineage3; sen0414_ch11ch12_lineage_v1_8_0.ttl: Lineage4; sen0414_ch13ch14_lineage_v1_5_0.ttl: Lineage5) and the slides register (sen0414_slides_lineage_v2_402_0.ttl: Lineage2, Lineage3, Lineage4, in its own, different IRI namespace). True next-free ordinal package-wide is 6, with no new collision this time (unlike the Lineage3/Lineage4 case). This lineage takes ordinal 6.

STATE-CHECK PRECEDING THIS OPENING (done before any stage was written, per the draft-first/state-check-first discipline used for Lineage3-5): chapters 15-16 were found to have a materially different build history than chapters 9-14. Both chapters went through a real repair/restart cycle in late October 2026, under the OLD iteration-20 structural-retrofit process (TK_Ret_Ch15_*, TK_Ret_Ch16_*), recorded Done in the closed slides lineage (Lineage2) before this lineage opened: chapter 15's page build failed its leak probe on all five seeds at v9_96_0 (log control-iter20-logs/leak_ch15_v9_96_0_template_9_52_4_FAIL_controller_run.log) and was repaired to v9_96_1, which the controller's own re-run confirms PASS on all five seeds (control-iter20-logs/leak_ch15_v9_96_1_template_9_52_4_controller_run.log) and which also passes page checks 9.34/9.37 (control-iter20-logs/pagechk_Page_Ch15_v9_96_1_run1-3.log, RESULT Page/Ch15: PASS); chapter 16's deck went through an intra-task re-commit (v2_0_0 superseded by v2_0_1, the deck actually controlled and delivered per TK_Ret_Ch16_Deck_Build's audit note), and its page build failed page test 9.37.0 at 1366px (P1, P9 overflow) at v9_96_0 (control-iter20-logs/p37_ch16_v9_96_0_t37_FAIL_controller_run.log) and was repaired to v9_97_0 with a narrower Playground starter file, which passes the leak probe, the width check at 1366/1400/390px, and page checks 9.34/9.37 (control-iter20-logs/leak_ch16_v9_97_0_template_9_52_4_controller_run.log, width_ch16_v9_97_0_controller_run.log, pagechk_Page_Ch16_v9_97_0_run1-3.log, RESULT Page/Ch16: PASS). The lineage register's own control-verdict comments confirm TK_Ret_Ch15_Research, TK_Ret_Ch15_Deck_Build, TK_Ret_Ch15_Page_Build, TK_Ret_Ch16_Research, TK_Ret_Ch16_Deck_Build and TK_Ret_Ch16_Page_Build all Done, with no outstanding NOT MET finding against the current (latest) artifact versions. No legacy YA-suffixed duplicate decks were found for chapters 15-16 (unlike chapters 11-14), so there is nothing to retire on that front. The story-companion scripts self-check clean (sen0414_ch15_stories_v1_0_1.py: 5 stories; sen0414_ch16_stories_v1_0_0.py: 6 stories), and the current chapter-code manifests (chapter_code_ch15_v1_0_0.json, chapter_code_ch16_v1_0_1.json, naming the controlled v2_0_1 deck) both list 25 examples. One new item not seen for chapters 9-14 was found and is explicitly OUT OF SCOPE for this lineage, per the same boundary Lineage5 drew around the already-Done structural retrofit: each chapter also has a rdodi/ subfolder (03-materials/ch15/rdodi/, 03-materials/ch16/rdodi/) holding versioned (v1.0.0 through v1.0.3/v1.0.4) research/domain-ontology artifacts (a document in .docx and .ttl, domain ABox/TBox/SHACL files, a research file) produced under the earlier iteration-20 process; these are a separate research/domain-modelling artifact set, not part of the deck+page+story+code+resources material this narrow-lineage pattern reviews, and are left untouched unless the owner says otherwise."""@en .

## --- Profile declaration (ceremony step 1) ---

ex:ProfileDecl6 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3, Lineage4 and Lineage5: work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work and this lineage names none other. Level L2 stated plainly because this lineage does not re-run the full SHACL/register tooling used by the BRSF framework's own self-governance against this course repository's simplified lineage files." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-11T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date .

## --- Lineage ---

ex:Lineage6 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 15 and 16, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission6 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 6 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl6 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed SEN0414 slides lineage this continues from, same as Lineage3, Lineage4 and Lineage5 before it. Chapters 15 and 16's structural retrofit (TK_Ret_Ch15_*, TK_Ret_Ch16_*) was recorded Done in that closed lineage, after a real repair cycle (see the ontology-level comment above), before it closed; no open defect is carried forward, only the pedagogical-review mission stated fresh here, parallel to, not continuing, Lineage3, Lineage4 or Lineage5."@en .

## --- Mission ---

ex:Mission6 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 15 and 16 taught from one approved draft each"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog6 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Chapters 15 (Google Sheets) and 16 (SQLite Databases) of the third edition are taught with a deck and an interactive page, each produced from one owner-approved chapter draft, following the same review given to chapters 9-10, 11-12 and 13-14: a true, sourced, pedagogically-motivated story per concept the chapter actually teaches (per the owner's 2026-11-09 principle - story count is not preset, but important history of the concepts must be covered within time and scope), an accurate resources slide, and any open items named and closed before build." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction this conversation, 2026-11-11 ('Let's proceed with next 2 chapters in order'), following the Lineage3/Lineage4/Lineage5 pattern and their own stated exclusion that later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages, rather than widening any earlier mission." .

## --- Scope (taxonomic: areas, deliverables, exclusions - G194) ---

ex:Scope6 a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    rdfs:label "Draft, check and (on approval) render chapters 15-16 only"@en ;
    backlog:scopeForMission ex:Mission6 ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_OwnerStated ; backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:coversArea ex:Area6_StateCheck, ex:Area6_Draft, ex:Area6_Render ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion ex:Excl6_Ch1to14, ex:Excl6_OtherChapters, ex:Excl6_ExamWork, ex:Excl6_RenderBeforeApproval, ex:Excl6_StructuralRetrofit, ex:Excl6_Rdodi ;
    backlog:hasScopeDeliverable ex:Del6_ApprovedDraft, ex:Del6_CheckedMaterials ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: for chapters 15 (Google Sheets: installing and setting up EZSheets, Spreadsheet objects, Sheet objects, Google Forms, Google Sheets quotas) and 16 (SQLite Databases: spreadsheets vs. databases, SQLite vs. other SQL databases, creating databases and tables, CRUD operations, rolling back transactions, backing up databases, altering/dropping tables, joining tables with foreign keys, in-memory databases and backups, copying databases, SQLite apps) of the 3rd edition only - (a) read the existing deck, page, research/ABox, the two chapters' already-self-checked story-companion scripts (sen0414_ch15_stories_v1_0_1.py, sen0414_ch16_stories_v1_0_0.py) and say plainly what is stale, missing, or duplicated against the owner's 2026-11-09 story principle and current resources-slide standard; (b) write one plain-text chapter draft per chapter (story per 5N1K using the real, already-sourced companion-script beats, explanations, slide outline, page-tab outline in slide order, each non-network code example with its executed result and each network/browser example checked for syntax and documented-library correctness, resources slide) for the owner's reading and approval; (c) ONLY after approval, render the deck, page and document from that one draft, versioned per the 2026-11-08 version rule (each file its own step, sized to the change). OUT: chapters 1-14 (chapters 1-8 midterm scope untouched; chapters 9-10 are Lineage3's own mission, 11-12 are Lineage4's own mission, 13-14 are Lineage5's own mission, none widened here); chapters 17 and onward (later narrow lineages, same pattern); exam and mock-exam work (held outside this repository); rendering before the owner's approval of the draft; the iteration-20 structural chapter-check/retrofit for chapters 15-16 (TK_Ret_Ch15_*, TK_Ret_Ch16_*), already Done (after its own repair cycle) in the closed Lineage2 and not reopened without a found defect; the rdodi/ research-and-domain-ontology artifact set under 03-materials/ch15/rdodi/ and 03-materials/ch16/rdodi/, a separate artifact family from the deck+page+story+code+resources material this lineage reviews." .

ex:Area6_StateCheck a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "What exists for chapters 15-16 today"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 .
ex:Area6_Draft a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "The one approved draft per chapter"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 .
ex:Area6_Render a backlog:ScopeArea ; rdfs:label "Deck, page and document rendered from the approved draft"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 .

ex:Del6_ApprovedDraft a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Owner-approved plain-text draft, chapters 15 and 16"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area6_Draft .
ex:Del6_CheckedMaterials a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; rdfs:label "Chapter-15/16 materials checked against current standard, gaps named"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:deliverableForArea ex:Area6_StateCheck .

ex:Excl6_Ch1to14 a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 1-14"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Chapters 1-8 are midterm scope, untouched; chapters 9-10, 11-12 and 13-14 are Lineage3/4/5's own closed missions, none widened by this lineage." .
ex:Excl6_OtherChapters a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Chapters 17-25"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages, same pattern as this one, Lineage3, Lineage4 and Lineage5." .
ex:Excl6_ExamWork a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Exam and mock-exam work"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Held outside this repository." .
ex:Excl6_RenderBeforeApproval a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "Rendering a deck/page/document before the draft is approved"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Same draft-first rule applied in Lineage3, Lineage4 and Lineage5: layout built before content is settled was the measured cause of the five-build-per-page slowness." .
ex:Excl6_StructuralRetrofit a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "The iteration-20 structural chapter-check/retrofit for chapters 15-16"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "Already recorded Done in the closed Lineage2, after its own real repair cycle (ch15 page leak-probe failure repaired v9_96_0 to v9_96_1; ch16 page overflow-at-1366px failure repaired v9_96_0 to v9_97_0; ch16 deck v2_0_0 superseded by v2_0_1). Reopening it without a found defect would be re-litigating a closed, controller-confirmed finding; this lineage's state-check (Area6_StateCheck) is the narrower, pedagogical-story-and-resources check only." .
ex:Excl6_Rdodi a backlog:ScopeExclusion ; rdfs:label "The rdodi/ research-and-domain-ontology artifact set for chapters 15-16"@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage6 ; backlog:hasExclusionRationale "A separate, versioned research/domain-modelling artifact family (document, domain ABox/TBox/SHACL, research files) under 03-materials/ch15/rdodi/ and 03-materials/ch16/rdodi/, not part of the deck+page+story+code+resources material this narrow-lineage pattern reviews; found during the state-check and left untouched pending the owner's direction." .
